{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1287972-how-do-you-decide-the-mechanics-of-a-fetish","id":1287972,"title":"How do you decide the mechanics of a Fetish?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-14T09:33:25-08:00","id":1287972,"title":"How do you decide the mechanics of a Fetish?","content":"So with a Talisman you simply take the normal Mage rules but roll the Arete of the object. A violin that conjures up a Forces 5 firestorm follows all the normal rules.<br /> <br /> What about a Fetish? The effects they're given are spirit powers using Gnosis, and they don't correspond to a specific &quot;Magick&quot; effect. If you tie a Fire Elemental into a ruby ring to give a fire blast power, how do you roll for it?<br /> <br /> - Mage rolls Willpower against the Spirit's Gnosis, both difficulty 6.<br /> <br /> - Assuming they succeed, the ring rolls its Gnosis, against... a difficulty. What difficulty?<br /> <br /> - The ring gets 3 successes. Is it like a Forces fire attack with 3 successes? A Spirit charm with 3 successes?<br /> <br /> This distinction can make huge differences. The Healing charm of a spirit rolls Gnosis difficulty 6 (Lethal) or 8 (Aggravated), and heals one damage per success. It can only be used on a certain character each scene. If you had that power in an amulet then that would be very different from having the Fetish just use the Life healing effects (that is, use the Damage/Success chart but replace Damage with points of health healed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-14-2019, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}